# CODEOWNERS — required-reviewer routing (CODE-QUALITY-STANDARD CQ-39, CI-CD-STANDARD
# CICD-17/18). This file has no effect on its own; it becomes load-bearing only once
# branch protection / a repository ruleset requires review from the matched code
# owner. The live `protect-main` ruleset does not require code-owner review today —
# it has no pull-request rule at all — so this routing is intent, not enforcement.
# The committed mirror of that ruleset is `.github/rulesets/main.json`, and closing
# the gap is issue #79.
#
# Solo-maintainer repo today: every path routes to the same owner. The workflow and
# safety-critical paths are named explicitly anyway so the intent (these paths
# always require the maintainer's own review, even if co-maintainers are added
# later) is legible from the file itself, not just from there being one name in it.

